{
  "manufacturer": "Measurlogic",
  "manufacturer_slug": "measurlogic",
  "model": "DTS family energy sub-meters (DTS 101/105/305/310/SMX/SKT/DC)",
  "model_slug": "dts",
  "short_model": "DTS",
  "aliases": [
    "DTS 101",
    "DTS 105",
    "DTS 305",
    "DTS 310",
    "DTS SMX",
    "DTS SKT",
    "DTS DC"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Energy meter",
  "applies_to": "Measurlogic DTS AC and DC sub-meters and transducers with Modbus RTU or Modbus TCP, per DTS Modbus Map version 2.7U (Oct 2012). Registers depend on model and wiring.",
  "summary": "The DTS family are compact DIN-rail, panel and socket energy sub-meters and transducers for single-phase, three-phase and DC circuits. Every value is a signed 32-bit integer in two holding registers, low word first. This map covers voltages, currents, frequency, power, power factor, unbalance, nett and split energy counters, identity and CT/PT ratio registers, and the RS-485 settings.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU",
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 100,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "1-based",
    "note": "Section 2.1.1 says the published addresses are 1-based in the 4x region; subtract 1 for the wire address (Voltage_LN_1 11001 -> 11000). Some masters want the 4 prefix (411001)."
  },
  "default_word_order": "CDAB",
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "DTS Modbus Map",
    "doc_number": "Version 2.7U",
    "revision_date": "2012-10-17",
    "url": "https://cdn.logic-control.com/docs/measurlogic/Measurlogic%20DTS%20Modbus%20Map%20V2.7U.pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 3-4 (registers, word order, power/energy resolution), pp. 5-9 (measurement and other registers)",
    "unofficial": true
  },
  "notes": [
    "Measurlogic does not host this map publicly that we could find; this copy is on a distributor's document CDN and is the unaltered Measurlogic document (Measurlogic header and footer on every page).",
    "All registers are signed 32-bit values with the LO register at the listed address and the HI register next (CDAB).",
    "Power, demand and energy registers have a variable resolution: engineering value in W / VA / var / Wh = raw x EnerPowDivider (register 16045) x 0.001. Their scale is therefore left at 1 and units blank; read 16045 once and apply the formula.",
    "Energy registers roll over after 999,999,999 counts.",
    "Min/max registers (116xx / 122xx), single-cycle currents, I/O channel status/coils (15301+), the output command register 40001 and the SunSpec map at 50001 are left out.",
    "Default Modbus address is 100 (on Modbus TCP it is always 100).",
    "Power factor registers (11100-11107) are left out: the manual marks their format 'Special' without defining it."
  ],
